# FREIRAUM article publishing

When creating or updating a **published full article**, SEO is mandatory and must be **static HTML** (visible in `view-source`), never JS-only.

## Required workflow

1. Put metadata in `articles.js` (`seoTitle`, `seoDescription`, `image`, `imageAlt`, `author`, `date`, `dateModified`, `topics`, `tags`, `href`, `published`).
2. Run the central generator:

```powershell
# New article (also inserts into articles.js)
.\tools\publish-article.ps1 -New -Id "..." -Title "..." -Teaser "..." `
  -BodyFile ".\drafts\....body.html" `
  -Image "assets/images/....jpg" -ImageAlt "..." `
  -Topics "..." -Tags "..." -SeoTitle "..." -SeoDescription "..."

# After editing articles.js for an existing page
.\tools\publish-article.ps1 -SyncId <id>

# Regenerate SEO heads for all full articles
.\tools\publish-article.ps1 -SyncAll
```

3. Validate before push:

```powershell
.\tools\validate-articles.ps1
```

Do **not** report an article as finished if validation fails.

## Rules

- Canonical / OG / Twitter / JSON-LD use `https://magazin-freiraum.de` only (never `kaisy84.github.io`).
- One cover field: `image` (no separate SEO image system).
- `dateModified` only for real content edits.
- Author: `Redaktion FREIRAUM` → Organization; named author → Person.
- Fallbacks: missing `seoTitle` → `[title] | FREIRAUM`; missing `seoDescription` → `teaser`.
